From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: touchscreen: nt36532: add the panel

The NT36532 is one chip for the panel and the touch controller, and a
reset of the panel also stops the controller. Add a reference to the
panel, so that the driver can start the controller after it.

---
 .../bindings/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml      | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml
index e1625d2..08d668c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml
@@ -61,6 +61,12 @@ properties:
       GPIOs that read the panel ID straps. The first GPIO gives bit 0 of the
       index into firmware-name.
 
+  panel:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      The panel on the same chip. A reset of the panel also stops the touch
+      controller, which then has to start again after the panel.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
